<title>BELGIUM: Fire hits Belgian ALZ steel plant - agency.</title>
<headline>Fire hits Belgian ALZ steel plant - agency.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>A fire late Tuesday at Belgian stainless steel maker ALZ NV, a unit of the Arbed group, has caused hundreds of millions of Belgian francs of damage, Belga news agency reported on Wednesday.</p>
<p>A spokesman for Sidmar NV, ALZ's Belgian parent company, was not immediately available to confirm the report or provide details of the fire.</p>
<p>ALZ produced 485,000 tonnes of stainless steel in 1995 and was due to increase that to 700,000 tonnes by the end of 1997.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
